# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.docker.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REAL FINANCIAL DATA — never commit.
# Everything under data/ is generated locally by the backend (holdings,
# transactions, trade history, account values, etc.) and contains live account
# information. It is intentionally NOT versioned: the app reads it at runtime
# and falls back to the bundled example dataset (lib/example.ts) when absent.
# Ignore the whole folder, not just *.json: a non-JSON write (a bridge's
# per-account subfolder and .bak backups, or anything else dropped in here)
# would otherwise slip past a *.json-only rule. This also already covers
# nested per-source subdirectories (e.g. data/snaptrade/) — the
# OptionsEvaluator side's multi-account merge writes a snapshot.json per
# brokerage source, not just at the top level — since git ignores a matched
# directory's entire contents, not just files matching the pattern directly.
# The .gitkeep keeps the empty folder so a fresh clone/Pi has somewhere to write.
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep

# Windows Explorer folder-settings artifacts
desktop.ini
**/desktop.ini
